<Layout title="Import and Update an Existing CV" active="guides"><main id="main" class="content-page article"><a href="/guides/">← All career guides</a><h1 style="margin-top:30px">An old CV can be a useful starting point.</h1><p class="lead">Import your existing document to recover its text, then review and organize it into a fresh template.</p><h2>What GlobalCV can read</h2><p>Choose a text-based PDF, a DOCX file or a plain text file up to 5 MB. PDF imports support up to 15 pages. The document is processed in your browser; the original file is not uploaded to our server.</p><h2>What importing does not promise</h2><p>Importing does not preserve your original design. Multi-column documents can have an unexpected reading order, and scanned pages need optical character recognition first. Names, dates and section boundaries may need correction.</p><h2>Review before replacing your current resume</h2><p>The review screen shows detected contact information and the full extracted text. Check both. You can edit the text and extract again. After importing, visit each editor section and split grouped employment or education details into individual entries.</p><h2>Keep the facts; improve the presentation</h2><p>Remove outdated or irrelevant material, verify every date and focus your descriptions on the role you want. Do not add skills or outcomes just because they appear in another person’s example.</p><h2>Download when you are ready</h2><p>Choose a template and download a free PDF. No account is required. If you want to return to your draft on another device, sign in and save it to your account.</p><a href="/" class="button primary">Open the resume builder →</a></main></Layout>
